+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `billing/invoice.py`:
+  - `Line.vat` used `unit_price * rate`, ignoring quantity. It now uses `net * rate` (PRICING.md rule 3).
+  - `Invoice.add` now raises `ValueError` for a rate name not in `RATES` (rule 3). Before, the error only surfaced later, or never.
+- `tests/test_invoice.py`, `test_reduced_rate_small_item`: this test was wrong, so I changed it. It expected VAT 0.02 and gross 0.52 for a 0.50 item at the reduced rate. 0.50 × 0.05 = 0.025, and rule 4 says round half up (0.025 becomes 0.03). The expected values are now 0.03 and 0.53. The code already rounded correctly. Please confirm finance agrees with that reading.
+
+## Verified
+- Before the change, `python -m unittest` failed 4 of 6 tests.
+- After the change, `python -m unittest` reports `Ran 6 tests ... OK`.
+- I checked the expected values in the other tests by hand against PRICING.md. They match.
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- I did not change `docs/PRICING.md` or any other file.
+- No tests cover half-up rounding on the net sum, or non-integer quantities.
